en torment and  mage if it exists may be consensual and  positive and ongoing partly because of  the positive way Ella sane talks  the Mormont she-bears meeting in the  woods and partly because of the way  torment talks about the woman who lives  nearby  it sounds like an ongoing relationship  but also because an ongoing consensual  relationship could better explain majors  daughter's torment says that the she  bear bears him Cubs children  maybe these are majors daughters those  of the mysterious unknown father  tormund also mentions sons which might  mean that mage is the mother of some of  tormance four sons it sounds almost as  though mage chooses to keep her five  daughters but gives her sons to be  raised by tormund beyond the wall though  it's hard to imagine how mage could do  all of this secretly this is a lot of  kids to come from a secret relationship  across the bay of ice so maybe only some  of the kids are the children of tormund  with mage but even if it's only some  that could be very significant mage and  torment may not be the first wildling  non wildling relationship in the series  there's Jon and Ygritte and Gilly and  Sam but mage Mormont is the lady of Bear  Island a ruler in the north if her kids  have free folk blood in them if Liliana  Mormont is half wildling that could  really impact the attitudes of people in  the North who of course mostly hate  wildlings bridging this gap between the  wildlings and the Northman is becoming  more important with White Walkers on the  way and any relationship between tormund  and mage could maybe help with this  alliance the hatred between tormund and  wildlings also adds a layer of tragedy  to a relationship between torment and  mage they're separated by sides that  have been enemies for centuries  star-crossed like Romeo and Juliet with  the montagues and capulets  and of course by dance tormund and major  split further apart  tormund is at Castle black while mages  way down in the neck possibly involved  in a northern conspiracy the lovers are  now so far apart would that I could find  her again  tormund says so look there's no strong  evidence for a relationship between  tormund and mage Hallman's story may be  just a story and majors daughters may  have been fathered by  common man on their Island or something  but the hints and connections with  strong bad-tempered she bears are there  and the logistics and timing could work  so it is at least fairly possible that  husband two bears torment and the  she-bear mage Mormont get together on  one cold winter's night thanks for  watching this video  if you'd like to help a team of  academics in their study of the Game of  Thrones fandom go take their  questionnaire at the link below thank  you to the patrons for making this video  possible including the Lisa C Williams  Bret Jensen Ziggy folksmen gavin biggs  tagout Mac Stone Neil Roop Ram Roop Lori  to lava and full astern thanks also to  Pauline on Twitter Cheers
 

